course: dictionary
lesson: 9860
title: Places of worship
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can work out a new word from the words around it. «The synagogue is the Jewish place of prayer and study, and a rabbi is a teacher and leader.» The sentence tells you what a synagogue is used for: prayer and study.
explain: Look at the words in the list around it. «In a church, mosque, synagogue, temple or gurdwara, speak quietly, do not run, and follow its rules.» These are all places of worship, so a synagogue must be a building where people worship.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put "a building where Jewish people meet to pray" in place of synagogue. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Synagogue» means a building where Jewish people meet to pray, study and gather as a community.
fact: «Torah» means the first five books of the Hebrew Bible, handwritten on scrolls that are read in the synagogue.
fact: A «rabbi» is a teacher and leader, and services in a synagogue are often led by a rabbi.
fact: Other places of worship include a church for Christians, a mosque for Muslims and a gurdwara for Sikhs.
exercise: «The synagogue is the Jewish place of prayer and study.» What is a synagogue? | A shop that sells bread and cakes | A school for very young children | A hospital for sick people | *A building where Jewish people meet to pray and study
exercise: «The Torah is handwritten on scrolls that are read in the synagogue with great respect.» What is the Torah? | A type of musical instrument | A kind of food eaten at weddings | *The first five books of the Hebrew Bible | The name of a famous rabbi
exercise: «In a church, mosque, synagogue, temple or gurdwara, speak quietly.» Why should you speak quietly in a synagogue? | Because it is a sports hall for games | Because the shops are closed | Because everyone there is asleep | *Because it is a place of prayer and respect
test: «The rabbi spoke kindly to the families at the synagogue.» What does a rabbi do? | Drives the buses in town | *Teaches and leads | Sells food and drinks
test: Which of these is a place of worship? | Cinema | Hospital | *Synagogue | Library
exam: «In a church, mosque, synagogue, temple or gurdwara, follow its rules, such as covering your head.» What does follow its rules mean? | Ignore the rules because you are a visitor | *Keep to the rules of that place | Break the rules because they are boring | Make up your own rules for the visit
